  "accessionCode": "CCX-A-31047",
  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A flat slab of beach stone with a shallow worked hollow, carrying a dried residue of ground sweep purple, shell lime and oil in the hollow and in a spill down one side. The pigment is used to dye grade bands and to mark stones for restacking, and it stains the hands of anybody who grinds it for a fortnight, which is regarded as part of the work. Deep in the midden, under about a metre of shell, with the muller stone lying beside it. The residue was still soft enough in the centre to sample.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
